 {"id":"CF-238","title":"GitHub App mode is only half landed: GITHUB_AUTH_MODE=app, the docs section and the selftest arm still sit on wt/cf-ghapp","status":"pending","priority":"P1","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-05: e693942 landed the four self-contained files (setup, token minter, refresh, example env) because a rebase onto a moved main would have conflicted in docs/MVP-PLAN.md, scripts/bunker-provision.sh and tests/selftest.sh. The remaining 400-odd lines of the original work are intact on branch wt/cf-ghapp at 54ba48d (1 commit, based on ff8e23a): the provisioner's GITHUB_AUTH_MODE=app wiring, the SKILL section with the permission table, the MVP-PLAN entry, and a 269-line selftest arm. Until they land, provisioning can only use a long-lived token, and nothing proves the app path end to end.","acceptance_criteria":"1. scripts/bunker-provision.sh accepts GITHUB_AUTH_MODE=app|token and, in app mode, mints an installation token before the bundle is built and installs the refresh so the node does not lose push rights at the one-hour mark.\n2. A selftest arm proves the refusals: absent key file, key at 644, a token that cannot read the repo (403), and an --check that never passes vacuously.\n3. specs/HARNESS.md or the bunker SKILL carries the permission table with a reason per permission, and a doc states the expiry risk in the operator's words.\n4. The commit that closes this row names 54ba48d as its source and states what was changed during the merge, so the disk-as-received branch and the landed result are both traceable.\n5. No file is landed that still contains a __pycache__ artifact: the original branch staged scripts/__pycache__/github-app-token.cpython-314.pyc and it must not reach main.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T03:47:41Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T03:47:41Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"61a64b557e67e4c5952e4ed06c7d847f1d665ff155bf6482286275bef44bc113"},"capability_tags":[],"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker