 {"id":"CF-239","title":"node_env.py refusals escape as an uncaught traceback and exit 1 — the same code it uses for drift, so a refusal reads as a failed check","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":1,"reasoning":"Found while documenting the script for sheet 3.2 and reproduced: plan_config runs at scripts/node_env.py:509, after the handler that ends at :506, so the refusals at :352-356 ('carries an inline value this editor does not model') and :358-361 ('appears twice') are raised outside the handler and surface as a Python traceback with exit 1. Measured: a profile with the same section twice prints 'Refusal: gateway: appears twice (lines 1 and 3)' and exits 1 — indistinguishable from --check's exit 1 for drift, and a traceback where every other refusal is a named row.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Both refusals are caught and printed in the script's own row format, naming the section and the line numbers, and never as a traceback.\n2. Refusal and drift are distinguishable by exit code: a refusal is exit 2 (the code the argparse path already uses) and --check drift stays exit 1.\n3. A second entry point that calls plan_config cannot reintroduce the leak: the handler covers the call site, not just the earlier one.\n4. A selftest leg feeds a duplicated section and an inline value and asserts the named row and the exit code, proven red by mutation.\n5. Sheet 3.2's CAUTION is updated from 'documented' to 'fixed' in the same change.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T04:01:48Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T04:01:48Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"3c194b4d9e16024b636446b60aaccab1a7e94a92bff50cda759b0d32b58d3e04"},"capability_tags":[],"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null}
 {"id":"CF-240","title":"install-opencode.sh's non_interactive row can never pass: it greps stdout while opencode writes --help to stderr","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":1,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-05 by the conformance battery: the adapter runs 'opencode --help' and greps its stdout for the non-interactive marker, but the binary writes that text to stderr, so the row cannot go green on any host — a check that cannot pass is decoration (AGENTS.md rule 2). Measured: 'opencode run --help' exits 0 and its text arrives on stderr.","acceptance_criteria":"1. The row reads both streams (or captures 2>&1) and prints the measured value it matched.\n2. A fixture proves the row goes RED when the binary stops advertising non-interactive mode, and GREEN against the pinned 1.18.29.\n3. The adapter says which version it measured and refuses a v2 request in writing (CRIER-HARNESS-10), since one id serves both generations today.\n4. No other adapter greps stdout alone for a capability it did not capture: the same class is swept in the change.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T04:15:37Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T04:15:37Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"8a28f967ffa74457820a5562a8a0b392920ebde77afea57fb5348ef0f9ba4c66"},"capability_tags":[],"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null}
+{"id":"CF-241","title":"P3 — CF-206 shipped a patch nothing can apply: its target `fleet_ops_check.py` exists in no commit, so AC6's `git apply --check` exits 1 and the only reproduction artifact for the unversioned census fix is inert","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-05T11:44Z by tick code-factory-duckbrain-qa-2026-11-05-11-35-44 at origin/main tip 81dd425e5bb6961ea596f3a8a194bd8647001821, tracked porcelain clean, origin/main...HEAD = 0 0, no operation markers, no live judge in this checkout.\n\nCF-206 was closed complete at 2026-11-05T00:33:05Z against d227effd (evidence run 18ef167d, guard PASS, Tier2 PASS). Its acceptance criterion 6 requires three conjuncts: the patch exists, `git apply --check patches/fleet-ops-shell-toolkit.patch` succeeds at the fixing HEAD, and the closeout quotes its sha256.\n\nConjunct 2 does not hold at the tip, nor at either of the row's own commits:\n\n- `git apply --check patches/fleet-ops-shell-toolkit.patch` -> `error: fleet_ops_check.py: No such file or directory`, rc=1.\n- The patch header is `--- a/fleet_ops_check.py` / `+++ b/fleet_ops_check.py`, so its target is a repo-root path.\n- `git cat-file -e d227effd:fleet_ops_check.py` -> absent; `git cat-file -e dc9e0ea:fleet_ops_check.py` -> absent; `git ls-files | grep -c fleet_ops_check` -> 0.\n\nThe artifact's CONTENT is honest; what is missing is a base and a stated location. Roundtrip measured in a scratch copy of the live file: reverse-applying the patch to ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py exits 0 and yields sha256 b0054326771850a85e2240a00f89935a3817ab864d445779740a92c2de3f2e9d — the pristine file the closure itself cites — and re-applying it restores the live file byte-for-byte (live sha256 82a3bf3418f1f521e3941334d796e09e1088512eb0f75ddd89d468d36f81d976). So the delta is captured exactly; there is simply no file in any commit for it to apply against, and no statement of where to run it.\n\nThe failure mode CF-206 did not test: nothing in the repo applies, documents, or drift-checks the patch. `grep -rn 'patches/' --include=*.sh --include=*.py --include=*.md scripts/ tests/ docs/ README.md AGENTS.md` -> 0 hits. `patches/fleet-ops-shell-toolkit.test.py` grades classify() fixtures (10 arms) against a module path passed on argv; it never touches the patch. Because the fixed module is unversioned, a hand-copied diff is the only thing keeping the census honest: regenerate or revert ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py and `--project code-factory --json` silently returns `docs` again while every gate stays green.\n\nArms of CF-206 that DO reproduce at this tip (recorded so the reopen stays scoped to AC6): AC0/AC1 `python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py --project code-factory --json | jq -r '.[0].kind'` prints `cli`, rc=0; AC2 `.[0].evidence.kind_basis` prints `shell-toolkit:15` (the closure quoted 8 — 16 tracked *.sh landed between d227effd and 81dd425, so the count moved with the tree rather than against the claim); AC5 the fleet census prints cli=7 docs=40 library=4 service=34 unknown=3, matching the recorded before/after.\n\nBoundary: CF-206 owns the census classification and is reopened only for its AC6 reachability claim. This row owns the artifact: a base the patch can apply against, a documented apply procedure, and a drift gate that goes red when the live file stops matching the shipped patch.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree, from the repository root (this is the row's probe): it prints `patch=patches/fleet-ops-shell-toolkit.patch target=fleet_ops_check.py target_at_head=absent apply_check_rc=1` and exits 0 today.\n1. The patch has a base it can apply against: the path its own header names exists at HEAD (`git cat-file -e \"HEAD:<target>\"` -> present) and `git apply --check patches/fleet-ops-shell-toolkit.patch` exits 0 at the fixing HEAD. The AC0 probe then prints `target_at_head=present apply_check_rc=0`.\n2. Applying the patch to that shipped base reproduces the patched module byte-for-byte: the result's sha256 equals a digest recorded in the repository for the patched module (ship it beside the base, e.g. `patches/`, and quote it in the closeout).\n3. A drift gate exists and can fail: a committed `scripts/verify-patch.sh` (or an arm in `tests/selftest.sh`) compares the shipped patch's roundtrip digest against the live `~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py` and prints a NAMED `FAIL` row when they differ. Prove both arms — unchanged live file: PASS row, exit 0; one byte appended to a COPY of the live file, with the copy passed to the gate: named `FAIL` row, nonzero exit, no traceback.\n4. The apply procedure is documented where a stranger finds it: the patch header or `patches/README.md` states the target path, the apply command and the working directory, and the documented command is the one AC1 runs.\n5. Gates green at the fixing tip: `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` rc=0 and `scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK`.\n6. The gate does not mutate fleet state: the live file's sha256 is identical before and after the AC3 negative-control run.","probe":"p=patches/fleet-ops-shell-toolkit.patch; t=$(grep -m1 '^+++ b/' \"$p\" | sed 's|^+++ b/||'); printf 'patch=%s target=%s target_at_head=%s apply_check_rc=' \"$p\" \"$t\" \"$(git cat-file -e \"HEAD:$t\" 2>/dev/null && echo present || echo absent)\"; git apply --check \"$p\" >/dev/null 2>&1; printf '%s\\n' \"$?\"","created_at":"2026-11-05T11:39:12Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T11:39:12Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"01e3d16383d9e1d779786ffd1213a9568f4ba1d5b3a9fc7a9afcf4494e6f8b76"},"capability_tags":[],"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null}
